---- session 3
 {90}*
 {90}* This is the compiler; cc.s, in assembly, is the bootstrap compiler that
 {90}* can compile it (lang/cc/DESIGN.md, section 6). It is written in the C it
 {90}* compiles, and within what a StrataOS program has: 40 KiB of data Local
 {90}* Store for its tables (symbols, types, the value stack), the arena behind
 {90}* far_read / far_write for everything large (the source text, identifiers,
 {90}* macros, fixups and the image being built). With lang/cc/host/ in place of
 {90}* StrataOS the same file is the cross compiler, build/strata-cc.
 {90}*
 {90}* One pass, no tree. Expressions leave descriptors of values on a value
 {90}* stack (a constant, a register, an lvalue not loaded yet, a comparison not
 {90}* made yet, pending jumps); code is emitted when an operation needs a value
 {90}* in a register.
 {90}*
 {90}* For the bootstrap compiler's sake: functions are defined before they are
 {90}* used where that is possible, and each compiles to less than 4 KiB.
 {90}*/
{34}#include {35}<strata.h>

{90}/* ---- the arena (offsets); 0x10000..0x4FFFF hold this program's own code units
{34}#define {}A_PT     {32}0x00000        {90}/* the parameter types of function types, 4 byte
{34}#define {}A_CS     {32}0x01000        {90}/* the cases of the switch statements open, 16 b
{34}#define {}A_IDH    {32}0x02000        {90}/* identifier hash heads, 4 bytes each */
